{title: 107 - God Moves in a Mysterious Way}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #107 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 107}
{meta: category God the Father - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D/F#]God moves [G/D]in [A/E]a [D]mysterious [Em/B]way
[D/A]His [A]wonders [G]to [A/E]perform;
[F#m]He [D/A]plants [A]His [Bm/F#]footsteps [F#m]in [E]the [A/E]sea,
[F#m]And rides [D/F#]upon [A/E]the [D/F#]storm.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D/F#]Ye fearful [A/E]saints, [D]fresh [A]courage [Em/B]take;
[D/A]The [A]clouds [D/F#]ye [G]so [A/E]much [D/F#]dread
[F#m]Are [D/A]big [A]with [Bm/F#]mercy, [F#m]and [E]shall [A/E]break
[F#m]In [A7/G]blessings [E7]on [A/E]your [D/F#]head.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D/F#]Judge not [G/D]the [A/E]Lord [D]by [A]feeble [Em/B]sense,
[D/A]But [A]trust [D/F#]Him [G]for [A/E]His [D/F#]grace;
[F#m]Behind [A]a [Bm/F#]frowning [F#m]providence
[F#m]He hides [D/F#]a [E7]smiling [D/F#]face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D/F#]His purposes will [A]ripen [Em/B]fast,
[D/A]Unfolding every hour;
[F#m]The [D/A]bud [A]may [Bm/F#]have [A/E]a [F#m]bitter [A/E]taste,
[F#m]But sweet [A7/G]will [D/F#]be [E7]the [A/E]flower.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D/F#]Blind unbelief is [A]sure [D/A]to [Em/B]err,
[D/A]And [A]scan [D/F#]His [G]work [A/E]in [D/F#]vain;
[F#m]God [D/A]is [A]His [Bm/F#]own [A/E]interpreter,
[F#m]And [A7/G]He [D/F#]will [E7]make [A/E]it [D/F#]plain.
{end_of_verse}
